<title>FINLAND: LIPPONEN SAYS FINNISH EMU POLICY UNCHANGED.</title>
<headline>LIPPONEN SAYS FINNISH EMU POLICY UNCHANGED.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister Paavo Lipponen said on Thursday Finland's policy on European economic and monetary union (EMU) was unchanged and not affected by domestic day-to-day politics.</p>
<p>&quot;Prime Minister Paavo Lipponen emphasises that the policy conducted by Finland on economic and monetary union has not changed. The day-to-day political discussion does not affect this policy,&quot; he said in a statement.</p>
<p>Lipponen said he issued the statement in response to a Reuters news story on Wednesday about his visit to Germany.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
